  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (photocopy-thin): Light photocopy, 1-bit: low binarisation threshold so only the darkest ink survives - staff lines, stems, ledger lines, slurs and hollow noteheads thin out and break up. mild thr 115, scan thr 85, severe thr 70 + patchy faded ink + 0.6 deg skew + toner dust. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Severe: some staff-line segments, ledger lines, ties and lyric hyphens/extenders vanish completely; the truth still contains them."
